        "original_id": "1ea770fa-250f-5697-8652-57078070ae89",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Harvey Jewell, Marshall Jewell, Ulysses S. Grant\n- Roles: Governor of Connecticut, United States Postmaster General, U.S. Minister to Russia, Republican Party National Chairman\n- Topics: manufacturing, telegraphy, telephony, politics\n\nFacts:\n- Marshall Jewell was born on October 20, 1825, and died on February 10, 1883.\n- Marshall Jewell was the younger brother of Harvey Jewell.\n- Marshall Jewell was a manufacturer, pioneer telegrapher, telephone entrepreneur, world traveler, and political figure.\n- Marshall Jewell served as the 44th and 46th Governor of Connecticut.\n- Marshall Jewell served as the 25th United States Postmaster General under President Ulysses S. Grant.\n- Marshall Jewell served as the U.S. Minister to Russia and as Republican Party National Chairman.",
